{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"title":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"type":"text","text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"archetype"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sparseSet"},{"type":"text","text":" storage (see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"How results are made trustworthy","anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each revision is built once and measured in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"faster"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"slower"},{"type":"text","text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"equivalent"},{"type":"text","text":", anything else as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Read and reproduce","anchor":"Read-and-reproduce","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest published report: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":". Reports are published for dedicated benchmark releases only; the page shows the newest."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2.0.0 report: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/"},{"text":", the full suite with 10 replicates on both storages. Its source is committed as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/BenchmarkReport.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under ","type":"text"},{"code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main:2.0.0 REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"sh"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER"},{"type":"text","text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.create.no-entities"},{"type":"text","text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark-report"},{"type":"text","text":" renders the single file "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BenchmarkReport.html"},{"type":"text","text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/README.md"},{"type":"text","text":" for all options."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Benchmarks","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ComponentMacro":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro","title":"Generating components with the component macro","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro"},"https://fireblade-engine.github.io/ecs/benchmarks/2.0.0/":{"title":"FirebladeECS 1.4.3 vs 2.0.0","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FirebladeECS 1.4.3 vs 2.0.0"}],"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","url":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEvent"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","title":"NexusEvent"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage","title":"Choosing a storage","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","iden